Hi Pat,

A line is order by the x values.  If you want to order by something
different, using the path geom and the order aesthetic.

Hadley

On Sat, Sep 19, 2009 at 3:38 PM, Pat Schmitz <p.sc...@gmail.com> wrote:
> The x axis is a continuous value, labeled value.
>
> The Y axis is a categorical orderd factor, labeled variable
>
> the geom_line() should plot the continuous value points along the
> categorical value.
>
> Where instead it is plotting the categorical variable along the continuous
> value.
>
> Pat
>
