I've been using geom_rect() to produce rectangles that convey the
error in the x and y directions simultaneously, together with
geom_point() to portray the estimate; e.g.

ggplot(bm, aes(x=PPmedian, y=SFP5median)) +
 geom_point() +
 geom_rect(aes(xmin=PPX10.0., xmax=PPX90.0.,
  ymin=SFP5X10.0., ymax=SFP5X90.0.), colour=alpha("black",1),
  fill=alpha("black",0))

