Subject: Re: missing data when axis limits set
Message-ID: <6yUkgOMESHo.k03KtnUcCKAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <6yUkgOMESHo.i1nETubTCaIJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
References: <6yUkgOMESHo.2KVg7-Z0OfkJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com> <6yUkgOMESHo.i1nETubTCaIJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/6yUkgOMESHo/m/k03KtnUcCKAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Right, this is a slightly unintuitive aspect of ggplot. The scale_
(limits=) syntax restricts the *data* (as do its unfortunately named
synonyms xlim and ylim), while the coord_(xlim=) syntax restricts the
*viewport*. Scale_ functions affects the mapping between data and
plot, while coord_ functions just change the plot. In retrospect, some
of these functions and parameters perhaps should have been named
something else...

 -Harlan

